"/services/gcc/jeddah-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Jeddah</a>, <a href="/services/gcc/doha-beauty-cosmetics-agency.php" style="color:#db2777;font-weight:700;">Doha</a>, Abu Dhabi, Dammam, Al Khobar, Kuwait City, Manama, Muscat, Ras al Khaimah). Every framework below is grounded in live category work.</div><p>Skincare SEO is different from generic e-com SEO. Buyer queries decompose across 6 dimensions (concern + ingredient + product + skin-type + routine + budget). Specialist skincare SEO delivers compounding organic engine that becomes 20-40% of revenue by month 24.</p>
                                    <h2>What skincare SEO specifically requires</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>6-dimension keyword architecture (concern + ingredient + product + skin-type + routine + budget)</li><li>Long-tail commercial-intent focus ("niacinamide serum for oily skin under 1000")</li><li>Certification + trust content (CDSCO + ingredient safety)</li><li>Comparison content depth (ingredient A vs B + brand A vs B)</li><li>Product + LocalBusiness + Review + AggregateRating schema</li><li>AI Overviews + ChatGPT + Gemini optimisation</li><li>Regional-language SEO (Hindi + Arabic + regional where audience justifies)</li></ul><p>Missing = 40-60% below achievable ranking + conversion.</p>
                                    <h2>Specialist vs generic agency evaluation</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Published skincare SEO case studies (real brands + ranking screenshots + organic revenue)</li><li>Skincare silo architecture examples (live sites with 6-dimension silo)</li><li>Skincare content library depth (20+ skincare playbooks published themselves)</li><li>Schema deployment expertise (Product + Organization + LocalBusiness + Review + Article + FAQPage)</li><li>AI Overviews citation-optimisation approach (answer-first + structured lists + entity clarity + llms.txt)</li><li>Regional-language SEO capability</li><li>Attribution + reporting (organic revenue tied to content + silo pages)</li><li>Content cadence + team capacity (6-10 pieces / month Growth-tier)</li></ul>
                                    <h2>Generic e-com SEO agency red flags</h2>
                                    <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Category-only silo (no 6-dimension)</li><li>Head-term targeting ("skincare" vs "niacinamide serum for oily skin")</li><li>Generic content templates ("10 skincare tips" listicles)</li><li>Missing certification content</li><li>Minimal schema (Organization + Product only)</li><li>No AI Overviews approach</li><li>English-only content</li><li>Vanity reporting (impressions + rankings only, no organic revenue)</li></ul>
                                    <h2>Cost + timeline &amp;mdash; specialist vs generic</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Specialist skincare SEO agency:</strong></p><ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;"><li>Retainer: Rs 1-3 lakh / month</li><li>Timeline: 6-10 pieces / month + 40-80 silo pages over 12-18 months + 100-200 content library over 18-24 months</li><li>Outcome month 12: 15-25% monthly revenue from organic. Month 24: 20-40%</li><li>Compounding: SEO investment compounds. Month 12 investment still delivering month 30-36</li></ul><p><strong>Generic e-com SEO:</strong> Rs 40K-1.5L / month. 3-8% monthly revenue by month 12. Weaker compounding.</p><p>Specialist 2-3x cost but 4-8x organic revenue over 24-36 months. Math favours specialist by year 2+.</p>
                                    <h2>ITD skincare SEO approach</h2>
